    [Doc][Misc] Update Kimi-K2.6 deployment documentation (#19783)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Clarify the Kimi-K2.6 deployment guide.
    
    - Keep only A3 and A2 Docker installation tabs; remove the 950DT
    products tab.
    - Use `/data/media` for local media access and explain the parameter.
    Describe scenarios where balance scheduling can increase TTFT.
    - Recommend a shared directory for `launch_online_dp.py` and
    `run_dp_template.sh` and explain their invocation relationship.
    - Number PD deployment steps consistently as 1, 2, and 3 in both
    Markdown and rendered output. Keep Decode parameter descriptions outside
    the node tabs, and place the proxy command in a `proxy.sh script` tab.
    - Remove duplicate single-node verification, clarify service port `8000`
    versus proxy port `1999`, and use address/port placeholders.
    - Normalize quantized model naming while retaining repository prefixes,
    service aliases, and draft model names. Remove the legacy DFlash YaRN
    compatibility paragraph.
    
    Only `docs/source/tutorials/models/Kimi-K2.6.md` is changed. The support
    matrix is excluded.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No. Documentation only; no runtime code, API, or configuration behavior
    changes. No release note fragment is required.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Passed: `.venv-docs/Scripts/python.exe -m mkdocs build --site-dir
    .vaws-local/kimi-k26-ci-fix-main`.
    - Passed: Git whitespace checks and local rebase onto the target branch
    snapshot.
    - Rebuilt as a single signed-off commit on the current target branch to
    avoid the CI rebase conflict from historical support-matrix commits.
    - Local Markdown rendering verified the three consecutive PD steps and
    Decode descriptions outside tabs.
    - Existing unrelated anchor warnings remain in the documentation build.
    - `bash format.sh ci` cannot complete locally because `pre-commit` is
    unavailable; remote CI will validate formatting.
    - No NPU/runtime tests were run for this documentation-only change.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
    Signed-off-by: CuiZ2007 <zhengcui2007@outlook.com>

